 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "c-tilde",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book writes the tilde here. The state that is not normalized is $|\\kpsi_\\alpha(\\kt+\\delta\\kt)\\rangle$ of Eq. (6.10), without it; the tilde marks the normalized state of Eq. (6.17)."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-table-step-3",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book writes $|\\tilde{\\phi}_{k,\\alpha}\\rangle$ with a $k$ the test does not fix. With $K$ running from $0$ and an empty sum taken as zero, the test $\\sum_{k=1}^{K}\\kdeltapk \\leq r < \\sum_{k=1}^{K+1}\\kdeltapk$ selects the channel $K+1$, so $|\\kpsi_\\alpha\\rangle$ is replaced by $|\\tilde{\\phi}_{K+1,\\alpha}\\rangle$."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-table-step-7",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book divides by $N$ but sums over the initial states only. The average runs over the $N$ trajectories of each initial state as well: $\\krhoS(\\kt) = \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_\\alpha p_\\alpha\\sum_{n=1}^{N}|\\kpsi_\\alpha^{(n)}(\\kt)\\rangle\\langle\\kpsi_\\alpha^{(n)}(\\kt)|$, where $|\\kpsi_\\alpha^{(n)}(\\kt)\\rangle$ is the $n$th trajectory started from $|\\kpsi_\\alpha\\rangle$."
  }
 ],
